# CMS Minimum Acceptable Risk Standards for Exchanges (MARS-E) 2.0 — Volume III: Catalog of Minimum
# Acceptable Risk Security and Privacy Controls for Exchanges, Version 2.0, November 10, 2015.
# An overlay of NIST SP 800-53 Rev 4 for ACA Administering Entities (Exchanges/Marketplaces, state Medicaid and
# CHIP agencies, Basic Health Program agencies). One attested row per control / enhancement table in Volume III.
#
# Source (Volume III, the catalog):
#   https://www.cms.gov/CCIIO/Resources/Regulations-and-Guidance/Downloads/3-MARS-E-v2-0-Catalog-of-Security-and-Privacy-Controls-11102015.pdf
#   sha256 1d8888a60ca582daf55ed6161ac38401604f8f4edaea4e2746d7067ce075708c, 348 pages, retrieved 2026-10-14.
# Baseline flags (Volume II, Appendix A "Security Controls Selection Table", Tables 3-20):
#   https://www.cms.gov/CCIIO/Resources/Regulations-and-Guidance/Downloads/2-MARS-E-v2-0-Minimum-Acceptable-Risk-Standards-for-Exchanges-11102015.pdf
#   sha256 1a031a48c66ae15d5d79a5ea72c921eda6f9175ad71fb006996e1e292776e051, retrieved 2026-10-14.
# CMS federal work: no copyright notice in either volume; US Government work (17 U.S.C. 105), public domain.
#
# STATUS (checked 2026-10-14): SUPERSEDED. MARS-E 2.0 was followed by MARS-E 2.2 (a state exchange site hosts
# "MARS-E-v2-2-Vol-1_08032021.pdf"; not downloaded, no cms.gov copy found) and both are replaced by
# ARC-AMPE — Acceptable Risk Controls for ACA, Medicaid, and Partner Entities, Version 1.0 (released 2025-03-04,
# compliance date 2026-03-04). The CMS CCIIO Regulations and Guidance page
# (https://www.cms.gov/marketplace/resources/regulations-guidance, page sha256
# 3ebf578e432904749c24e3def4d0ffb82316309cbc8dc30df002e8608563864a) now lists only ARC-AMPE; the MARS-E 2.0 PDFs
# are still served at the unlisted CCIIO URLs above. This module is kept for historical/contractual assessments
# and for SCF crosswalks that still map MARS-E 2.0; new ACA assessments should use ARC-AMPE.
#
# Extraction (generator, text layer of the PDF; nothing paraphrased):
#   rows: 352 control/enhancement tables (Table 1 AC-1 .. Table 352 UL-2): 316 security controls in 18
#   families + 36 privacy controls in 8 families (Appendix A, IRS Publication 1075 FTI requirements, is not
#   catalog rows and is not included). id = the control number as printed in the body ("AC-2 (1)": a space
#   before the enhancement number, as every body table prints it; the List of Tables prints "CM-8(1)" once).
#   title = the table caption; text = the "Control" statement; implementation_standards = the "Implementation
#   Standards" cell. NIST guidance, related controls and assessment procedures are not carried.
#   The security rows match the "MARS-E V 2.0" column of Volume II Appendix A exactly (316 = 316, no difference).
#   Baseline flags from the same tables: nist_800_53r4_moderate, cms_ars_2_0, mars_e_1_0 = selected | not_selected
#   (privacy families have no selection table: n/a). They are data, not gates. Every expanded cell names its own
#   row's control except one: the CMS ARS V 2.0 cell of SC-ACA-1 reads "SC-CMS-1" (the ARS equivalent), so
#   SC-ACA-1 carries cms_ars_2_0 = not_selected by id.
# COULD NOT READ — text rendered as images: the PDF draws list items (a., b., 1., ...) and almost all
#   Implementation Standards as per-line images with no text layer. 224 of 352 rows have such image lines
#   (1691 lines in the Control and Implementation Standards cells); their count is carried per row as
#   image_lines_not_extracted, and the row text holds only the text-layer part (often just "The organization:").
#   47 rows have no text-layer control statement at all (text ""). Implementation Standards text was
#   extractable for 23 rows only. No OCR was applied; the id, title and attestation are unaffected.
# Source irregularities, kept or normalised as noted: Table 328 caption prints "D-1 (1)" (body header DI-1 (1)) and
#   Table 329's body header prints "D1-1 (2)" — both carried as DI-1 (1) / DI-1 (2); Table 337 (DM-3 (1)) caption wraps
#   and is joined; captions of AC-14, IA-5 (11), MP-6 (2), SI-2 (1) differ slightly from their body headers (caption kept).
#
# Families:
#   1.1   AC  Access Control                                        38
#   1.2   AT  Awareness and Training                                 5
#   1.3   AU  Audit and Accountability                              22
#   1.4   CA  Security Assessment and Authorization                 11
#   1.5   CM  Configuration Management                              26
#   1.6   CP  Contingency Planning                                  23
#   1.7   IA  Identification and Authentication                     18
#   1.8   IR  Incident Response                                     13
#   1.9   MA  Maintenance                                           12
#   1.10  MP  Media Protection                                      12
#   1.11  PE  Physical and Environmental Protection                 22
#   1.12  PL  Planning                                               6
#   1.13  PS  Personnel Security                                     8
#   1.14  RA  Risk Assessment                                        8
#   1.15  SA  System and Services Acquisition                       17
#   1.16  SC  System and Communications Protection                  34
#   1.17  SI  System and Information Integrity                      25
#   1.18  PM  Program Management                                    16
#   2.1   AP  Authority and Purpose                                  2
#   2.2   AR  Accountability, Audit, and Risk Management             8
#   2.3   DI  Data Quality and Integrity                             5
#   2.4   DM  Data Minimization and Retention                        6
#   2.5   IP  Individual Participation and Redress                   6
#   2.6   SE  Security                                               2
#   2.7   TR  Transparency                                           5
#   2.8   UL  Use Limitation                                         2
#
# Input: input.cms_mars_e.controls["AC-2 (1)"] == true means the Administering Entity attests that control or
# enhancement implemented as MARS-E 2.0 specifies. Fail-closed: a missing or non-object controls container is a
# FAIL-CLOSED violation; a missing, false or non-true value is a violation; an unknown id is a violation.
#
# Query: POST /v1/data/cms_mars_e/main/compliance_report

