	{"id": "SA-4", "family": "SA", "kind": "control", "title": "Acquisition Process", "text": "The organization includes the following requirements, descriptions, and criteria, explicitly or by reference, in the acquisition contract for the information system, system component, or information system service in accordance with applicable federal laws, Executive Orders, directives, policies, regulations, standards, guidelines, and organizational mission/business needs:", "implementation_standards": "As part of the service contract, the AE must establish security and privacy policies and procedures for how data is stored, handled, and accessed within service provider environment; The data must be encrypted in transit to and from the service provider environment; All mechanisms used to encrypt data must be FIPS 140-2 compliant, and operate using the FIPS 140-2 compliant module; and Storage devices where data has resided must be securely sanitized according to MARS-E MP-6 Media Sanitization security control prior to use. Per SA-9 (5), the outsourcing of information system services outside the continental U.S. must be authorized by the CIO of CMS.", "image_lines_not_extracted": 15, "nist_800_53r4_moderate": "selected", "cms_ars_2_0": "selected", "mars_e_1_0": "selected", "table": 228},
	{"id": "SA-4 (1)", "family": "SA", "kind": "enhancement", "title": "Functional Properties of Security Controls", "text": "", "implementation_standards": "", "image_lines_not_extracted": 2, "nist_800_53r4_moderate": "selected", "cms_ars_2_0": "selected", "mars_e_1_0": "selected", "table": 229},
